# ledger: research.db trials family=structure_wave_fwd_v1 dataset=gate_structure_fwd_2026-10-21 (registered 2026-10-21, N 58->60 together with structure_chart_fwd_v1)
# 2026-10-24 I-2026-10-24-01 (data integrity; additive — frozen .md unchanged). OPERATIONAL DECISION, not pre-authorised by the frozen text:
#   frozen §4 makes a data-integrity failure a kill condition ('판정불가'), and §3-4 ('데이터 공백 … 공백 비율 보고') concerns missing bars inside
#   resolution windows — neither covers corrupt log rows. Fact: 8 of the first 11 wave_log rows had a close different from the exchange's final close
#   (truncated last candles of v1 pagination / in-progress snapshots promoted from the 1 h pickle); the 3 1d rows' frames held a fake bar too.
#   Rule (mechanical, outcome-blind): every row with logged_at < meta.loader_v2_live_ts (first start of the fixed loader, set once) is listed in
#   wave_log_quarantine and treated as NOT LOGGED — the frozen data model already allows missing rows (view-dependent logging, §6). Quarantined rows are
#   excluded from scoring and churn; wave_log itself is untouched (first-log-only). Hypothesis, constants and event definitions are unchanged;
#   wave_T0 stays 1792555200 (12-month deadline unchanged).
#   Re-basing: an id whose first record is quarantined is scored from its first non-quarantined row (new t0 and that row's inv/target/close/p_ref);
#   the report gives n_rebased and the max lag in bars (server _wave_scored exposes both). Under the RW null this is unbiased because scoring restarts
#   at the new t0 with that row's own inv/target/p_ref (Markov property); the selection rule itself ignores outcomes.
#   No 4h event could mature before ~2026-11-07, but resolutions before maturity (target/invalidation touched in the first bars) may have been visible on
#   the chart when the rule was fixed — neutrality rests only on the rule ignoring outcomes. Any residual integrity failure found at judgement still
#   means 판정불가 (frozen §4).
# P1b hourly job (logged_by 'job', in-process thread in the SYSTEM dashboard, polls every 60 s, logs each new closed bar 75 s after close):
#   live from 2026-10-24T12:00:08Z (meta.job_live_ts, read from the live structure.db on 2026-10-27; dashboard process started 2026-10-24T12:00:01Z
#   = meta.loader_v2_live_ts); meta.job_live_ts = logged_at of the first wave_log row the job actually INSERTED (set once — a job attempt on a bar a
#   view already logged does not set it). Rows are written only for the 3-symbol pool (BTC/ETH/SOL USDT perps), only after the quarantine migration
#   succeeded (otherwise the write is withheld and retried), never while structure.db is locked at the deploy-marker read (withheld, counted as a log
#   failure, retried by the next view/job poll), and only from frames that pass the quality gate (not the 1000-bar fallback, reached the present, latest
#   closed bar <= 1 bar late, no zero-volume flat among the last 3 closed bars or at a re-fetched page junction, no missing bar among the last 3, no
#   re-fetched page-junction bar absent from the response — R5-DL-L1 2026-10-27; other flats / other missing bars are warnings only).
# 2026-11-03 A 27-cell job (additive — frozen .md unchanged): wave_log rows are gateio-only by the new exchange gate in server_api._forward_log_append
#   (_WAVE_LOG_EXCHANGE = 'gateio'; applies to views and to the hourly job alike). The job now also runs binance/bybit cells (27 cells, gateio first) for
#   the display cache, the weekly RW controls and the closed-bar archive; those cells write no wave_log row and never set wave_T0 / wave_T0_meta /
#   job_live_ts (their status is read-only: wave.skipped_kind 'exchange', counted neither as a log failure nor in cells_logged). Before this change the
#   pool check alone would have let a binance view write an exchange=binance row (none ever did). Verify FAILs on COUNT(wave_log WHERE exchange != 'gateio') > 0.
